:Namespace test_WebSockets
⍝ WebSocket tests for Jarvis
⍝ Usage:
⍝   From the shell (repository root):  dyalogscript Tests/WebSockets/run.apls
⍝   From an APL session with #.Jarvis loaded:  #.test_WebSockets.Run
⍝ Run returns a vector of failure messages; empty means every test passed.
⍝ Each test starts its own Jarvis on its own port, and uses a raw Conga client (Jarvis's own LDRC) that it
⍝ upgrades to a WebSocket, so the WebSocket handshake and frames can be driven directly.
⍝ See docs/plans/websockets.md for the behaviour these tests cover.
⍝ Ports: every server in a run gets its own port, BasePort+1, BasePort+2, ... (8291 and up by default); ports are
⍝ never reused within a run. If they clash with another process, set BasePort before calling Run, or set the
⍝ environment variable JARVIS_TEST_PORT for run.apls.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1
    CRLF←⎕UCS 13 10
    LF←⎕UCS 10
    BasePort←8290
    Verbose←1                ⍝ 1 = print each test's name and result as it runs

    TJarvisSource←':Class TJarvis: #.Jarvis' ':Field Public Logged←⍬' '∇ {msg}←{level}Log msg' ':Access public override' 'Logged,←⊂,⍕msg' '∇' ':EndClass'

    ∇ r←Run;tests;t;res
      :Access public
    ⍝ run every test_* function, returning a vector of failure messages
      r←⍬
      :If 9≠#.⎕NC'Jarvis'
          →0⊣r←,⊂'#.Jarvis is not loaded'
      :EndIf
      ⎕FIX TJarvisSource
      tests←{⍵/⍨'test_'∘≡¨5↑¨⍵}⎕NL ¯3
      PortsUsed←0
      :For t :In tests
          App←MakeApp
          (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
          :Trap 0
              res←⍎t
          :Else
              res←,⊂'errored: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM
          :EndTrap
          StopAll
          r,←(⊂t,': '),¨res
          :If Verbose
              ⎕←t,': ',(1+0∊⍴res)⊃('FAILED (',(⍕≢res),')')'passed'
              ⎕←⍪res
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

⍝ ─── the application code (CodeLocation) used by the tests ─────────────────────────

    ∇ app←MakeApp
      app←⎕NS''
      ResetState app
    ⍝ hook functions
      app.⎕FX'r←Upgraded ns' 'LastNs←ns' 'Ups,←⊂ns.conx' 'r←UpgradeResult'           ⍝ OnWsUpgradeFn
      app.⎕FX'r←UpReq ns' 'LastNs←ns' 'Ups,←⊂ns.conx' 'r←UpReqResult'                ⍝ OnWsUpgradeReqFn
      app.⎕FX'r←Recv ref;ns' 'ns←ref.##' 'LastNs←ns' 'Received,←⊂ref.Payload' '{}ns.conx ns.Server.WsSend''ack:'',ref.Payload' 'r←RecvResult' ⍝ OnWsReceiveFn
      app.⎕FX'r←OnClose ns' 'Closes,←⊂ns.conx' 'r←0'                                 ⍝ OnWsCloseFn
      app.⎕FX'r←Auth ns' 'AuthCalls+←1' 'r←AuthResult'                               ⍝ WsAuthenticateFn
      app.⎕FX'r←Init srv' 'r←0'                                                       ⍝ AppInitFn (a hook, for the built-in-handler exclusion test)
    ⍝ endpoint functions
      app.⎕FX'r←echo p' 'r←p'           ⍝ ordinary JSON endpoint, in IncludeFns
      app.⎕FX'r←secret p' 'r←''SECRET''' ⍝ ordinary JSON endpoint, NOT in IncludeFns
      app.⎕FX'r←a dyadicfn b' 'r←0'      ⍝ dyadic, for valence-rejection tests
    ∇

    ∇ ResetState app
    ⍝ (re)initialise the mutable state the hooks read and record, so sub-tests don't leak into each other
      app.UpgradeResult←0    ⍝ OnWsUpgradeFn result
      app.UpReqResult←0      ⍝ OnWsUpgradeReqFn result
      app.RecvResult←0       ⍝ OnWsReceiveFn result
      app.AuthResult←0       ⍝ WsAuthenticateFn result (0 = pass)
      app.LastNs←⍬           ⍝ most recent connection namespace seen by a hook
      app.Received←⍬         ⍝ payloads passed to OnWsReceiveFn
      app.Closes←⍬           ⍝ connections passed to OnWsCloseFn
      app.Ups←⍬              ⍝ connections passed to OnWsUpgradeFn / OnWsUpgradeReqFn
      app.AuthCalls←0        ⍝ number of times WsAuthenticateFn was called
    ∇

⍝ ─── helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Expect←{⍺:0⍴⊂'' ⋄ ,⊂⍵}                 ⍝ cond Expect 'message'  →  ⍬ if cond, else the message
    Contains←{∨/⍺⍷⍵}                        ⍝ 'needle' Contains 'haystack'
    LoggedMatch←{∨/∨/¨(⊂⍵)⍷¨⍺.Logged}       ⍝ j LoggedMatch 'text'
    Captured←{9=⌊⊃,App.⎕NC⊂'LastNs'}        ⍝ 1 if a hook has stored a connection namespace in App.LastNs

    ∇ j←NewServer dummy
    ⍝ create (but don't start) a test server on its own port with WebSockets enabled
    ⍝ the caller sets the hooks it needs before calling Start
      j←⎕NEW TJarvis
      j.Port←BasePort+PortsUsed←PortsUsed+1
      j.CodeLocation←App
      j.EnableWebSockets←1
      j.DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD←'debug'
      j.WaitTimeout←5000 ⍝ Stop allows the server this long to finish
      Servers,←j
    ∇

    ∇ StopAll;j;c
    ⍝ stop every server this test started and close its clients
      :For j :In Servers
          :Trap 0
              {}j.Stop
              {}j.LDRC.Close j.ServerName ⍝ in case the server was Reset rather than stopped
          :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      :For c :In Clients
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}#.Jarvis.LDRC.Close c ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
    ∇

    ∇ (c evt)←j WsOpen path;rc;w
    ⍝ open a raw client to server j, request a WebSocket upgrade for path, and return the client name and the
    ⍝ event the client received (WSUpgrade on success)
      (rc c)←2↑j.LDRC.Clt'' 'localhost'j.Port'http'10000('Options' 1) ⍝ client auto-upgrades
      'Could not connect'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨rc≠0
      Clients,←⊂c
      {}j.LDRC.SetProp c'WSUpgrade'(path'localhost' '')
      evt←3⊃4↑(j.LDRC.Wait c 3000),4⍴⊂''
    ∇

    ∇ j WsPut(c text)
    ⍝ send a text WebSocket frame from client c
      {}j.LDRC.Send c(text 1)
    ∇

    ∇ (evt text)←j WsRead(c ms);w;rc
    ⍝ wait up to ms ms for one event from the server on client c
    ⍝ evt is 'WSReceive', 'Closed' or 'Timeout'; text is the frame text for a WSReceive
      w←4↑(j.LDRC.Wait c ms),4⍴⊂''
      (rc evt)←w[1 3]
      :If rc=100 ⋄ (evt text)←'Timeout' '' ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf   ⍝ 100 = Conga Wait timeout
      :If rc≠0 ⋄ (evt text)←'Closed' '' ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf       ⍝ e.g. 1010 object not found → gone
      :If (⊂evt)∊'Closed' 'Error' 'WSClose' ⋄ (evt text)←'Closed' '' ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf
      text←(evt≡'WSReceive')/⊃4⊃w,⊂''
    ∇

    ∇ text←j WsReadData(c ms);end;evt;t
    ⍝ read from client c until one WebSocket message arrives (its text), the connection closes, or ms pass
    ⍝ tolerates the reply arriving a little late (the built-in handler replies from a task thread)
      end←ms+⎕AI[3] ⋄ text←''
      :While ⎕AI[3]<end
          (evt t)←j WsRead(c 300)
          :If evt≡'WSReceive' ⋄ →0⊣text←t ⋄ :EndIf
          :If evt≡'Closed' ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ text←j OneShot(path msg);c;evt
    ⍝ open a fresh WebSocket, send one message, return the single reply, and close
    ⍝ a fresh connection per message keeps the built-in handler's task-thread replies from drifting across messages
      text←''
      (c evt)←j WsOpen path
      :If 'WSUpgrade'≢evt ⋄ →0⊣text←'<no upgrade: ',evt,'>' ⋄ :EndIf
      j WsPut c msg
      text←j WsReadData(c 3000)
      {}j.LDRC.Close c ⋄ Clients~←⊂c
    ∇

    ∇ r←WaitFor(cond ms);end
    ⍝ evaluate the expression cond every 100ms, for up to ms milliseconds; r is 1 as soon as it's true
      end←ms+⎕AI[3]
      :Repeat
          :If ⍎cond ⋄ →0⊣r←1 ⋄ :EndIf
          {}⎕DL 0.1
      :Until ⎕AI[3]>end
      r←⍎cond
    ∇

⍝ ─── tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_Shutdown;j;t;res
    ⍝ Start then Stop returns promptly with WebSockets enabled
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsReceiveFn←'Recv'
      :If 0≠⊃res←j.Start
          →0⊣r←⊂'Start failed: ',⍕res
      :EndIf
      t←⎕AI[3]
      res←j.Stop
      r,←(res≡0 'Server stopped')Expect'Stop returned ',⍕res
      r,←(5000>⎕AI[3]-t)Expect'Stop took ',(⍕⎕AI[3]-t),'ms'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Startup;j;rc;msg
    ⍝ WebSocket hooks are valence-checked at start-up when EnableWebSockets is on
      r←⍬
    ⍝ a dyadic OnWsReceiveFn is rejected
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsReceiveFn←'dyadicfn'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'dyadic OnWsReceiveFn should be rejected'
      r,←((rc≠0)≤'is not a'Contains msg)Expect'rejection message should say "is not a ...": ',⍕msg
      {}j.Stop

    ⍝ a dyadic OnWsUpgradeReqFn is rejected (this hook is now valence-checked too)
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsUpgradeReqFn←'dyadicfn'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'dyadic OnWsUpgradeReqFn should be rejected'
      {}j.Stop

    ⍝ valid monadic hooks are accepted
      j←NewServer''
      j.(OnWsUpgradeFn OnWsReceiveFn OnWsCloseFn WsAuthenticateFn)←'Upgraded' 'Recv' 'OnClose' 'Auth'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc=0)Expect'valid WebSocket hooks should be accepted: ',⍕msg
      {}j.Stop

    ⍝ with WebSockets disabled, the hooks are not valence-checked
      j←NewServer''
      j.EnableWebSockets←0
      j.OnWsReceiveFn←'dyadicfn'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc=0)Expect'with EnableWebSockets←0, a dyadic OnWsReceiveFn should not be checked: ',⍕msg
      {}j.Stop
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_UpgradeAuto;j;c;evt
    ⍝ WsAutoUpgrade←1 (the default): Conga accepts, then OnWsUpgradeFn runs
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsUpgradeFn←'Upgraded'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'auto upgrade: client event ',evt,', expected WSUpgrade'
      r,←(WaitFor'0≠≢App.Ups' 3000)Expect'OnWsUpgradeFn should run'
      r,←(Captured ⍬)Expect'OnWsUpgradeFn should have been passed the connection namespace'

    ⍝ OnWsUpgradeFn returning non-zero closes the connection
      ResetState App
      App.UpgradeResult←1
      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(WaitFor'Captured ⍬' 3000)Expect'rejected upgrade: hook did not capture the connection'
      r,←(WaitFor'0≠⊃App.LastNs.conx j.WsSend ''x''' 3000)Expect'a rejected upgrade (OnWsUpgradeFn→1) should close the connection'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_UpgradeManual;j;c;evt
    ⍝ WsAutoUpgrade←0: the upgrade is decided by OnWsUpgradeReqFn, or accepted if there is none
      r←⍬
    ⍝ OnWsUpgradeReqFn → 0 accepts
      j←NewServer''
      j.WsAutoUpgrade←0 ⋄ j.OnWsUpgradeReqFn←'UpReq'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'manual upgrade, OnWsUpgradeReqFn→0: event ',evt,', expected WSUpgrade'
      {}j.Stop

    ⍝ OnWsUpgradeReqFn → non-zero rejects
      ResetState App
      j←NewServer''
      j.WsAutoUpgrade←0 ⋄ j.OnWsUpgradeReqFn←'UpReq' ⋄ App.UpReqResult←1
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed (reject case)'
      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      r,←('WSUpgrade'≢evt)Expect'manual upgrade, OnWsUpgradeReqFn→1: event ',evt,', expected not WSUpgrade'
      {}j.Stop

    ⍝ no OnWsUpgradeReqFn accepts every upgrade
      ResetState App
      j←NewServer''
      j.WsAutoUpgrade←0
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed (no hook case)'
      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'manual upgrade, no OnWsUpgradeReqFn: event ',evt,', expected WSUpgrade (accept all)'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Receive;j;c;evt;text
    ⍝ OnWsReceiveFn is dispatched the message, can send a reply, and its result controls the connection
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsReceiveFn←'Recv'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'upgrade failed: ',evt
      j WsPut c'hello'
      text←j WsReadData(c 3000)
      r,←('ack:hello'≡text)Expect'reply text ',(⍕text),', expected ack:hello'
      r,←((⊂'hello')∊App.Received)Expect'OnWsReceiveFn should have been passed the payload; got ',⍕App.Received

    ⍝ OnWsReceiveFn returning non-zero closes the connection
      App.RecvResult←1
      j WsPut c'again'
      r,←(WaitFor'0≠⊃App.LastNs.conx j.WsSend ''x''' 3000)Expect'OnWsReceiveFn→non-zero should close the connection'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Authentication;j;c;evt;text
    ⍝ WsAuthenticate runs before OnWsReceiveFn; failure closes without dispatch; success authenticates once
      r←⍬
    ⍝ failed authentication: the message is not dispatched and the connection closes
      j←NewServer''
      j.(OnWsUpgradeFn OnWsReceiveFn WsAuthenticateFn)←'Upgraded' 'Recv' 'Auth'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      App.AuthResult←1
      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'upgrade failed: ',evt
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(WaitFor'Captured ⍬' 3000)Expect'auth test: hook did not capture the connection'
      j WsPut c'blocked'
      r,←(WaitFor'0≠⊃App.LastNs.conx j.WsSend ''x''' 3000)Expect'failed authentication should close the connection'
      r,←(0=≢App.Received)Expect'failed authentication should not dispatch to OnWsReceiveFn; got ',⍕App.Received
      {}j.Stop

    ⍝ successful authentication happens once per connection, not per message
      ResetState App
      j←NewServer''
      j.(OnWsReceiveFn WsAuthenticateFn)←'Recv' 'Auth'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed (success case)'
      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'upgrade failed (success case): ',evt
      j WsPut c'one' ⋄ {}j WsRead(c 2000)
      j WsPut c'two' ⋄ {}j WsRead(c 2000)
      j WsPut c'three' ⋄ {}j WsRead(c 2000)
      r,←(WaitFor'3=≢App.Received' 3000)Expect'all three messages should be dispatched; got ',⍕App.Received
      r,←(1=App.AuthCalls)Expect'WsAuthenticate should run once per connection; ran ',(⍕App.AuthCalls),' times'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_BuiltinHandler;j;text
    ⍝ with no OnWsReceiveFn and the HTML interface on, the built-in handler runs a named endpoint,
    ⍝ honouring IncludeFns / ExcludeFns and the hook-function exclusion (CheckFunctionName)
    ⍝ each message uses a fresh connection, so one message's reply can't drift onto the next
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.HTMLInterface←1 ⋄ j.IncludeFns←'echo' ⋄ j.AppInitFn←'Init'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

    ⍝ a permitted endpoint runs and returns its result
      text←j OneShot'/' '{"Endpoint":"/echo","Payload":[1,2,3]}'
      r,←('[1,2,3]'Contains text)Expect'built-in handler should echo [1,2,3]; got ',⍕text

    ⍝ an endpoint excluded by IncludeFns is rejected
      text←j OneShot'/' '{"Endpoint":"/secret","Payload":0}'
      r,←(('Invalid Endpoint'Contains text)∧'secret'Contains text)Expect'an endpoint outside IncludeFns should be rejected; got ',⍕text

    ⍝ a hook function is rejected
      text←j OneShot'/' '{"Endpoint":"/Init","Payload":0}'
      r,←(('Invalid Endpoint'Contains text)∧'Init'Contains text)Expect'a hook function should be rejected; got ',⍕text

    ⍝ a malformed message is reported through ErrorInfo
      text←j OneShot'/' 'this is not json'
      r,←('WSReceive Error'Contains text)Expect'a malformed message should return a WSReceive Error; got ',⍕text
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_WsSend;j;c;evt;text;res
    ⍝ WsSend accepts a connection name or a connection namespace, and reports send failures
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsUpgradeFn←'Upgraded' ⍝ captures the connection namespace in App.LastNs
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'upgrade failed: ',evt
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(WaitFor'Captured ⍬' 3000)Expect'no connection namespace captured'

    ⍝ by connection name
      res←App.LastNs.conx j.WsSend'byname'
      r,←(0=⊃res)Expect'WsSend by name returned ',⍕res
      text←j WsReadData(c 3000)
      r,←('byname'≡text)Expect'client should receive "byname"; got ',⍕text

    ⍝ by connection namespace
      res←App.LastNs j.WsSend'byns'
      r,←(0=⊃res)Expect'WsSend by namespace returned ',⍕res
      text←j WsReadData(c 3000)
      r,←('byns'≡text)Expect'client should receive "byns"; got ',⍕text

    ⍝ sending to a non-existent connection fails and is logged
      res←'CON99999999'j.WsSend'nowhere'
      r,←((~0∊⍴res)∧0≠⊃res)Expect'WsSend to a missing connection should return non-zero; got ',⍕res
      r,←(j LoggedMatch'WsSend')Expect'a failed WsSend should be logged'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Disconnect;j;c;evt
    ⍝ when the client drops, the server cleans the connection up (Conga 'Closed' → RemoveConnection)
    ⍝ note: OnWsCloseFn fires on a WebSocket close handshake (WSClose), which a browser's ws.close() sends but a
    ⍝ raw Conga client here does not, so OnWsCloseFn itself is left to manual/browser testing
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer''
      j.OnWsUpgradeFn←'Upgraded' ⍝ captures the connection namespace in App.LastNs
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      (c evt)←j WsOpen'/'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←('WSUpgrade'≡evt)Expect'upgrade failed: ',evt
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(WaitFor'Captured ⍬' 3000)Expect'no connection namespace captured'
      {}j.LDRC.Close c
      Clients~←⊂c
      r,←(WaitFor'0≠⊃App.LastNs.conx j.WsSend ''x''' 3000)Expect'the server should remove the connection after the client drops'
    ∇

:EndNamespace
